      passed for 511 tickets; `git diff --check` passed.

## Children and review boundaries

- 1003 — runtime registration, installed entry points, guard wiring and safe
  operator documentation in PR #1091. The first independent gate found
  unsafe removal guidance and missed predecessor registration; fixes passed
  the final gate and PR #1091 merged. Child 1003 is closed. Installation/relocation fixtures preserve independent
  profiles; author live smoke covers Claude/Codex/Pi clean and dirty controls.
- 1002 — legacy helper handoff, closed WONTDO in PR #1099: superseded by
  memory v8. Its extracted patch stays historical and unapproved, not part of
  #1091 or a v8 implementation. 0934 retires provenance.py after verifying no
  current executable consumers; memory stores and source history are preserved.

The author requested removal of all migration-specific controls: historical
pointer/path-spelling ratchets and old-layout tests are removed from the
registration slice. Current functional installation and guard tests remain.
No real runtime profile is deployed and no memory data is migrated here.

## Remaining work

1. Runtime registration landed through closed child 1003 in PR #1091, with
   smoke/trust limitations recorded and profile content preserved.
2. Child 1002 is WONTDO; do not implement its legacy helper contract or reconcile
   its store. 0988 retains safe v8 capture/integration; 0913 retains rollout.
3. Integration review is complete: registration landed in PR #1091, child 1002
   was closed WONTDO in PR #1099, and 0934's obsolete provenance helper was
   retired in PR #1101. The full suite passed (1225 passed, 2 skipped) against
   the integrated mainline. The memory v8 pilot tracked by 0920 is downstream
   work, not a prerequisite for this parent; 0988 and 0913 remain separate
   follow-on work.
4. Native packaging, runtime selection/dry-run and opt-in shell integration
   remain follow-on design work, not acceptance claims for child 1003.

## Actions

1. Make every harness-owned entry point derive the checkout from its own real
   location or an explicit root argument; never require `~/.idh` as a pointer.
2. Treat `~/.agents` as the documented default clone and runtime profile paths
   as adapter destinations only.
3. Inventory and remove canonical-path assumptions from code, tests and current
   documentation. Preserve runtime-native paths only where the runtime itself
   owns that path.
4. Define additive, idempotent registration for each supported runtime without
   replacing or owning the runtime's whole profile directory.
5. Verify the same checkout in a second arbitrary absolute location and through
   installed adapter links.

## Test

Run lifecycle, projection, shell-loader and adapter fixtures with a checkout
whose path is neither `~/.agents`, `~/.idh` nor `~/.claude`. Move that fixture
and rerun through the installed links. A hard-coded canonical repository path
must make the test fail.

## Exit criteria

- [x] A fresh clone at `~/.agents` installs supported adapters without a `~/.idh` pointer.
- [x] The same tests pass from an arbitrary checkout path and after that checkout moves.
- [x] Runtime profiles remain independently owned and existing unrelated content is preserved.
- [x] No current code or documentation describes `~/.idh` or `~/.claude` as the repository's canonical location.
- [x] `make check` passes and live smoke tests cover Claude, Codex and Pi registration.
